    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88473" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσᾰγωγ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>attractive, persuasive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ ἀκροάσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.21
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ αὑτοῦ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Def.</u>
					415a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσαγωγὸν μειδιᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DDeor.</u>
					20.11
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <i>exciting,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐπιθυμιῶν αἰσχρῶν τέχναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					2.28
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσαγωγεύς</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, prob. in Anon.Hist. (<i><span class="en">
				<u>FGrH</u>
				153
			</span></i>) <i><span class="en">
				p.825J.
			</span></i></div>
